Lab 1. Undercloud Architecture Overview
Objectives
Understand the role of the undercloud in OpenStack architecture
Identify key undercloud components and services
Learn how the undercloud orchestrates overcloud deployment
Gain hands-on experience with undercloud configuration
Prerequisites
Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8/9 system with 16GB+ RAM, 4+ CPU cores, 100GB+ disk
sudo/root privileges
Network connectivity (Internet access required)
Basic familiarity with Linux command line
OpenStack CLI tools installed (python3-openstackclient)
Lab Setup
Prepare your environment:
sudo dnf install -y python3-openstackclient git
sudo systemctl disable firewalld
sudo systemctl stop firewalld
Task 1: Undercloud Deployment and Configuration
Subtask 1.1: Install Undercloud Packages
sudo dnf install -y python3-tripleoclient git
Subtask 1.2: Create Undercloud Configuration
Create undercloud.conf:

cat <<EOF > undercloud.conf
[DEFAULT]
undercloud_hostname = undercloud.localdomain
container_images_file = containers-prepare-parameter.yaml
local_ip = 192.168.24.1/24
network_gateway = 192.168.24.1
undercloud_public_host = 192.168.24.2
undercloud_admin_host = 192.168.24.3
local_interface = eth1
network_cidr = 192.168.24.0/24
masquerade_network = 192.168.24.0/24
dhcp_start = 192.168.24.5
dhcp_end = 192.168.24.30
inspection_iprange = 192.168.24.100,192.168.24.120
EOF
Subtask 1.3: Deploy Undercloud
openstack undercloud install
Expected Outcome:

Undercloud services will be deployed in containers
You should see successful completion message
Verify with:
sudo podman ps
Task 2: Identify Critical Undercloud Services
Subtask 2.1: Verify Glance Service
source ~/stackrc
openstack image list
Expected Outcome: Should show available images (if any)

Subtask 2.2: Verify Heat Service
openstack stack list
openstack orchestration service list
Expected Outcome: Should show Heat engine is active

Subtask 2.3: Verify Ironic Service
openstack baremetal node list
openstack baremetal driver list
Expected Outcome: Should show available drivers (even if no nodes)

Task 3: Overcloud Orchestration
Subtask 3.1: Prepare Overcloud Images
openstack overcloud image upload --image-path /usr/share/rhosp-director-images/
Subtask 3.2: Create Overcloud Deployment Plan
openstack overcloud deploy --templates \
  -e /usr/share/openstack-tripleo-heat-templates/environments/network-isolation.yaml \
  -e ~/templates/network-environment.yaml
Subtask 3.3: Monitor Deployment
openstack stack list --nested
openstack stack events overcloud --follow
Troubleshooting Tips
If services fail to start:
sudo podman logs <container_name>
Network issues:
sudo ovs-vsctl show
ip a
Check service status:
sudo systemctl list-units "tripleo_*"
Conclusion
In this lab, you:

Successfully deployed an OpenStack undercloud
Identified and verified critical undercloud services (Glance, Heat, Ironic)
Prepared for overcloud orchestration
Gained practical experience with undercloud operations
